    "local_sha256": "faedd66920e11c920b69b81f1b5f77e2d74a024148815e3904e2c71d77f9c2f7",
    "modification": "Use scoped DNS-pinned HTTPX transport for gateway, dashboard login and cookie clients; deny redirects/proxies. Inspect exception fields carry backend_error_text (class code and the backend's own text, 0.2.0); explicit safe error boundaries (backend_errors) on every other handler, including late decoding/JSON failures, preserving signatures and successful output. 0.2.0: the W2b session/cron metadata projections are gone (upstream's own list output again); hermes_mcp, hermes_config, hermes_chat and hermes_webhook got the same error boundary. 0.2.2 (test VM 2026-10-16, G1): config reads redact backend-held credentials. redact_config replaces every non-empty value under a secret key (a word in SECRET_WORDS, or a last word in SECRET_LAST_WORDS: api_key, *_TOKEN, basic_auth; not max_tokens) with [REDACTED], nested objects and lists included, keeps field names, empty strings, null and booleans, and the password of a URL's userinfo; hermes_config get (whole config, or a key path: a secret part hides the whole value) and hermes_inspect's config_summary use it. Writes (set) unchanged. 0.2.2 (test VM 2026-10-16, G2): hermes_chat's POST /v1/responses may take CHAT_TIMEOUT (HERMES_MCP_CHAT_TIMEOUT, 1-3600 s, default 300; connect 30 s); _gateway_client takes the timeout, every other Gateway/Dashboard call keeps 30 s. Commercial acceptance AI-HMCP-001-1/-001-3/-002-2 (PaaS woow-mcp-server PR #68 has the same rules): ids and names put into dashboard URLs (session_id, job_id, webhook/toolset/MCP server names) must be one plain segment (letters, digits, _ . - : @ + ~, inner spaces; never '..', '.' or '/') and are percent-encoded, otherwise a JSON error and no request; hermes_config set normalizes the key (NFKC, format characters removed, strip, casefold, dot segments of [a-z0-9_-]) and refuses the denied roots (api_server, custom_providers, dashboard, mcp_servers, model, providers, secrets, security, terminal), every key under them and their ancestors, any secret segment and leading '_'; hermes_mcp add accepts only http/https URLs without userinfo whose resolved addresses pass backend_policy (resolve_async) and are not loopback/unspecified."
  },
